<!--
    GH-747: a return register written under a condition, then tested on the
    same condition again, lost the return value.

      twice:  cmp rdi,rsi; jae 1f; mov eax,0; 1: jb 2f; lea rax,[rdi+rsi]; 2: ret
      once:   the same logic with one branch
      differ: twice with a DIFFERENT second test (cmp rdx,rcx; jb)
      compl:  twice with the second test inverted (jae)

    The path "jae taken, then jb taken" reaches the RETURN with rax still the
    function's input.  It cannot run, but ActionReturnRecovery walks it before
    ActionConditionalExe threads the merge block away, and output trials get one
    pass, so twice printed void twice(void).  In differ and compl the input path
    CAN run (a0 >= a1 with a2 < a3, and a0 >= a1), so both must stay void with
    the option on.

    sfp is libgcc's void __sfp_handle_exceptions(int) from the mcount_x86_64
    fixture: xmm0 is written under bit tests of edi that are all different, so
    no merge branches on the condition that opened it and none is threaded.  A
    retry that re-judged the trial whatever happened to the merge found xmm0
    realistic on the next iteration (a later rewrite of its data-flow, not a
    removed path) and printed a value-returning sfp.

    comp puts the reporter's shape (test dil,0x40 / je / xorps xmm0 / jne ret)
    in FRONT of the same body, and comp2 puts it after the body.  The merge in
    comp is threaded, but with none of 0x40|0x1|0x4|0x20 set xmm0 still
    reaches the ret untouched, so both must stay void.  The retry is scheduled
    only when a walk that passes every such input finds all of them read in
    merges ActionConditionalExe can thread (in comp the body's merges are
    not), and the late walk fails at any input overlapping the recorded ones.
    comp and comp2 are relocated from 0x401000 to 0x501000 with their rodata.

    nested has two same-condition pairs in a row, so two merges must go before
    it returns 0, 1 or a0 + a1.

    Stage / sub-stage: P4 "output-prototype", option condexeret.  Pass 1 pins
    off (the bug), pass 2 the default.
-->
